{"chunk_id": "292dfb1b9b37", "text": "Manthara successfully poisons Queen Kaikeyi\u2019s mind against Rama. Kaikeyi angrily declares her intention to prevent Rama\u2019s coronation and asks how Bharata might instead gain power. Manthara reminds her of a past battlefield episode during a war between the devas and asuras: when King Dasaratha was wounded, Kaikeyi saved him, and he granted her two unclaimed boons. Manthara now urges her to use them\u2014demand Bharata\u2019s coronation and exile Rama for fourteen years so that people will forget him and accept Bharata\u2019s rule. She also instructs Kaikeyi to manipulate Dasaratha emotionally by lying in the \u201cchamber of wrath\u201d and refusing to speak until he renews his promise. Flattered by Manthara and convinced by her scheme, Kaikeyi commits fully to the plot that will trigger Rama\u2019s exile and the epic\u2019s central turning point.\nManthara convinces Kaikeyi to exploit two old boons from Dasaratha to exile Rama for fourteen years and install Bharata as ruler.\nThemes: manipulation, ambition for power, court intrigue, boons and vows, exile plot", "vector": [0.0032405774109065533, -0.017314916476607323, 0.0026572735514491796, -0.014163029380142689, -0.010615449398756027, 0.009755844250321388, -0.033156223595142365, -0.013678648509085178, -0.0214355681091547, -0.0011614911491051316, 0.012048126198351383, 0.0013917427277192473, -3.2885465770959854e-05, 0.03577597439289093, -0.00047542681568302214, 0.0015725328121334314, 0.053077246993780136, -0.0023127489257603884, 0.005017778370529413, -0.025651728734374046, 0.0027254961896687746, 0.0076545849442481995, -0.0020313304848968983, 0.01825639046728611, -0.03241942077875137, 0.006815446075052023, 0.02170845866203308, -0.03891421854496002, -0.004796054679900408, -0.008186722174286842, -0.0013738343259319663, -0.003078548703342676, 0.018556570634245872, -0.01444956474006176, -0.030591052025556564, 0.013528558425605297, 0.008009343408048153, -0.00016469381807837635